.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH orgsidian-index 1  "index " 
.SH NAME
orgsidian\-index \- Create, rebuild, inspect, or verify a vault\*(Aqs derived SQLite index
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBorgsidian index\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage a vault\*(Aqs derived SQLite index (LD\-49 rebuild\-index, LD\-27 CLI\-as\-integration\-surface).
.PP
`init` creates and populates the index (incremental on re\-run); `rebuild` drops it and re\-scans from scratch; `stats` prints counts, schema version, and the last\-indexed timestamp; `integrity` runs the SQLite and FTS5 consistency checks and exits non\-zero on any failure. The index lives outside the vault, under the OS data dir (or the ORGSIDIAN_DATA_DIR override). Each subcommand takes a <vault> path and an optional \-\-json flag that emits a single JSON object with no progress noise.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
orgsidian\-index\-init(1)
Create + populate the index for a vault (incremental on re\-run)
.TP
orgsidian\-index\-rebuild(1)
Drop the index and fully rebuild it from scratch
.TP
orgsidian\-index\-stats(1)
Print index statistics: counts, schema version, last\-indexed time
.TP
orgsidian\-index\-integrity(1)
Verify index integrity (SQLite + FTS5 consistency checks)
